# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# IMPORTANT: when this file exists it REPLACES .gitignore for the build archive.
# Anything .gitignore protects has to be restated here, or it starts getting
# uploaded — .env in particular, which holds DATABASE_URL.
#
# Do NOT add google-services.json: the Android build reads it via
# app.json → android.googleServicesFile.
#
# LEADING SLASHES MATTER. A bare `supabase/` matches at any depth, so it also
# excluded services/supabase — the entire Supabase API layer — and the build died
# with "Unable to resolve module @/services/supabase". Anchor anything that names
# a specific project directory.

# ── secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json
*service-account*.json
*serviceAccount*.json
dbrun.mjs

# ── build noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.git/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
.kotlin/
expo-env.d.ts
*.orig.*
.metro-health-check*
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
.DS_Store

# ── agent tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .claude/skills contains SYMLINKS into .agents/skills. EAS copies the working
# tree into a shallow clone and tries to recreate them, which fails on Windows
# without developer mode:
#   EPERM: operation not permitted, symlink '.agents/skills/…' -> '…/.claude/skills/…'
# None of it is app code, so it should never have been in the upload regardless.
/.claude/
/.agents/

# ── not part of the app ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 179MB of source art kept after optimisation — the shipped WebPs live beside
# them in assets/, and nothing in the app require()s these.
/assets/_originals/
# Store listing screenshots; not bundled (Metro only bundles require()d assets).
/assets/screenshots/
# SQL migrations and Deno edge functions — server-side, never in the APK.
/supabase/
# Privacy policy served from GitHub Pages.
/docs/
# Standalone HTML decks.
/presentations/

# ── generated native projects ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These only exist if someone ran `expo prebuild` locally. If they reach EAS,
# the build treats the project as BARE and uses the checked-in native code
# instead of regenerating it — which means every later app.json change (icons,
# permissions, plugins) silently stops applying. Always let EAS prebuild.
# LEADING SLASHES MATTER — see the note at the top of this file.
/android/
/ios/
